    "commit": "56eb1f83a3c5a6422cf54cdb0c58d16395934ab3",
    "commit_body": "market_breadth._get_daily_breadth now restricts the breadth universe to\nStock entries with non-null sector. ETFs in the DB (~45 entries) had been\ncontaminating breadth signals \u2014 leveraged 3x (TQQQ, SOXL, LABD, BOIL) in\nparticular were distorting advancing/declining counts and TRIN volume by\nmoving 3x the underlying index in either direction.\n\nAffects breadth_score \u2192 regime composite (35% weight) \u2192 Score.overall.\nRequires breadth-backfill + recalculate to propagate. ALGORITHM_VERSION\nbump in follow-up commit.\n\nAlso bundles infrastructure additions from this session:\n- monte_carlo.py: SAW Put U-curve env-overridable mechanism (default OFF;\n  Phase B/C Bayesian sweep tested it, FAILED P3+P4 portfolio gate, kept\n  in code as research apparatus). Production behavior unchanged when\n  SAW_PUT_UCURVE_ENABLED=0 (default).\n- trader.py: ETF_SYMBOLS extended with XLK/XLV/XLY/XLI/XLB/XLRE/SOXX\n  (six SPDR sector ETFs were missing from the skip-fundamentals set;\n  backfilled 2026-05-07 for sector-ETF screen analysis).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
    "commit_short": "56eb1f83",
    "commit_subject": "Filter ETFs from production breadth universe",
